    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DjHKVMQmvVnXWZYx2E2crb)_\n\nFollow-up to #46 (merged). Main was merged into this branch; conflicts were in `docs/architecture/load-order.org`, `docs/main.org` and `sp-relationship-annotator.org` (main's current late-module list and the `docs/architecture/` paths are kept).\n\n**Changes**\n- `lem--late-modules`, `lem--load-late-modules` and `lem--schedule-late-modules` are now `sp-late-modules`, `sp-load-late-modules` and `sp-schedule-late-modules` (init.el, docs, CHANGELOG, `sp-embr.org`).\n- `sp-ai` is out of the late list and is required at the end of `lem--default-modules`, so Claude's MCP servers are up as soon as the Emacs is.\n- `sp-ai` now declares `mcp-server-lib` first and calls `mcp-server-lib-start` in its `:config`; `vulpea-mcp-enable` runs from the `vulpea-mcp` `:config` (the top-level call failed because the package wasn't built yet); `org-mcp` is added and enabled.\n- `org-mcp` may change the `.org` files directly in `area/` and `inbox/` of the notes directory (`sp-org-mcp-files`, the same two folders as the agenda). That is write access for Claude: shorten the list if you want less.\n- `sp-ai.org` has a new section, \"Running the MCP servers without a GUI\": `emacs --daemon=mcp --headless-host`, then register `emacs-mcp-stdio.sh --server-id=… --socket=…` for `vulpea` and `org-mcp`, so no GUI Emacs is needed.\n- `load-order.org` and its SVGs follow: late list as in main, `sp-ai` in the startup group, `mcp-server-lib` edges, and the problems found.\n\n**Checked:** Emacs 29.3 reads `init.el` and `sp-ai.el`; `sp-ai.org` tangles to the same text as `sp-ai.el`; `sp-org-mcp-files` run against a temp notes directory; no conflict markers left; graphs re-rendered.\n**Not checked:** a real Elpaca startup or a real daemon (MELPA and Emacs packages aren't reachable here), so `org-mcp`'s API names (`org-mcp-enable`, `org-mcp-allowed-files`) come from its README, and the daemon recipe is untested.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015tcMWj1Z6j2uCgMRYPBfDN\n",
